<title>ITALY: Italian bonds/futures closing report.</title>
<headline>Italian bonds/futures closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian debt instruments extended gains in the run up to the close, tracking but outperforming other European markets, in bullish sentiment boosted by a firmer lira against the mark, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;Sellers were nowhere to be seen and now the December Liffe Btp has risen above 116.20 there's room to rise further,&quot; one traders said, putting next resistance at 116.45.</p>
<p>The lira firmed to near its day's high, quoted around 1,010.30 at the close, helped by the dollar's performance.</p>
<p>&quot;For now the market is ignoring any domestic political uncertainties,&quot; another treader said.</p>
